<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "benchmarked datasets" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Selected Problems" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "problem topics" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "designed prototype for evaluation" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "area (region) of land in which water is collected (drained) from higher altitudes to lower altitudes" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "catchment area" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "a hypothetical storm (rainfall event) characterized by temporal distribution of rainfall intensity, duration and return period, generally used for the purposes of design and analysis of hydraulic systems" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "design storm" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123013> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123013> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "duration of design storm (hypothetical storm, hence rainfall event, characterized by temporal distribution of rainfall intensities, duration and return period)" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "duration of design storm" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123014> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123014> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "real or estimated average period between two identical events such us water levels, discharges, eartquakes, etc." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "return period" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "parameters of any numerical model, which are used for calibration of model in order to optimize objective function or to meet some criterion" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "calibrated parameters" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "low impact development (LID) practices - practices applied in order to reduce flood risk in areas (usually urban areas), usually mimic natural hydrological and hydraulic processes. E.g. green roofs, rain barrels, permeable pavements, rain gardens, etc." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LID practices" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123017> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123017> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Most efficient of all LID practices analyzed in the research. LID is the abbreviation for low impact development, that is, name for practices applied for flood risk reduction in areas (usually urban), usually mimic natural hydrological and hydraulic processes" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123017> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "most efficient LID practices" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123018> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123018> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123018> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "return period of observed storm (rainfall event) or design storm (hypothetical rainfall event) " .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123018> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "return period of storm" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reduction of peak runoff achieved by some design or measure applied in order to reduce peak runoff and runoff volume in rainfall-runoff process. Those design or measures may include any hydraulic structure or practice (drainage, sewer, low impact development practices, etc.) applied to lower the flood risk. Reduction is usually expressed as percentage" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123019> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reduction of peak runoff" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123020> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123020> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reduction of total runoff volume achieved by some design or measure applied in order to reduce peak runoff and runoff volume in rainfall-runoff process. Those design or measures may include any hydraulic structure or practice (drainage, sewer, low impact development practices, etc.) applied to lower the flood risk. Reduction is usually expressed as percentage" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123020> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reduction of runoff volume" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123021> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123021> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Defines caracteristics of observed rainfall data (real, not simulated) or wether it was used for the analysis" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123021> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "observed rainfall event" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123022> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123022> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Defines characteristics of rainfall intensity-duration-frequency (IDF) curves obtained by using historical dataset of rainfalls, or wether it was used in research or not" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123022> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creation of IDF curves from historical data " .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123023> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123023> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Defines characteristics of rainfall intensity-duration-frequency (IDF) curves obtained by using output of the climate model (climate projections scenarios), or wether it was used in research or not, usually draws need of temporal and spatial downscaling in order to produce rainfall intensities for smaller area or location" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123023> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "creation of IDF curves from climate model output" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123024> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123024> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "defines wether or not hydrologic-hydraulic model was calibrated on observed rainfall events, or defines characteristics related to this calibration" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123024> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model calibration on observed rainfall event" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123025> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123025> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "defines wether or not hydrologic-hydraulic model was verified on observed rainfall events, or defines characteristics related to this verification" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123025> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model verification on observed rainfall event" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123026> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123026> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Define method used for multivariate frequency analysis, or wether multivariate or univariate frequency analysis was used, frequency analysis means probabilistic analysis of duration, return period (frequency) and intensities (magnitude) of phenomena, such us, water level, river flow, earthquake, rainfall, etc." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123026> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "multivariate frequency analysis" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123027> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123027> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "camera pose" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123028> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "segmentation" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123029> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The number of trajectories recorded and used in the research" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123029> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "trajectories" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The country where the research or development of the dashboard is based in or originated from." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dashboard developer country" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Primary - All resources by which the required data were directly obtained from healthcare centers, hospitals, clinics, primary care centers, medical records, individuals, etc. Secondary - All data obtained by other approaches, e.g., from existing or publicly available databases, government reports, media, web-scraping/web-crawling, etc." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "source of data" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123032> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Global - The data displayed by the dashboard belong to multiple countries.\nNational - The data displayed by the dashboard belong to a single country (national) or multiple states or provinces of a country.\nState - The data displayed by the dashboard belong to one or more counties/cities of a single state/province.\nCounty - Data displayed at a more detailed level compared to the state level, e.g., institutional\nlevel.\nOrganizational - Dashboards that belonged to one or more health institutes and/or organizations;\nsuch dashboards are mainly used only by the organizations in question." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123032> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "level of data granularity" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123033> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Death - The total and/or new number of fatalities caused by COVID-19.\nActive/new cases - Includes total confirmed cases and/or active/new cases, which may or may not include hospitalized patients. Critical and severe cases are considered separately as ancillary indicators.\nRecovered - Patients who have recovered from the infection\nTests - Negative/positive and/or total tests carried out on suspected patients." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123033> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "main indicators of COVID-19" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123034> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Patient status - Patients\u2019 clinical/physiological status (e.g., vital signs (heart rate, body temperature,\nrespiratory rate, blood oxygen saturation), abnormal symptoms (e.g., chest X-ray abnormalities), any laboratory and radiology tests, etc.).\nICU hosted - Any COVID-19 infected case with a severe clinical situation (normally defined by COVID-19 severity score) admitted to the ICU, hosted in ICU, or dead in\nICU.\nTests - Tests, test types, and any test result (positive or negative).\nDemographic data - Case identification data (e.g., age, sex, race, ethnicity, nationality).\nGeographic data - Any kind of data related to locations and population (e.g., city/state/region details, distance data, GIS data).\nPopulation data - Any population-related data (e.g., population demographics, travels data, occupational\ndata).\nHospitalized - Any case infected with COVID-19 hosted in the hospital to receive clinical care." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123034> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ancillary indicators of COVID-19 (other)" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123036> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123036> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123036> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "data sources" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123038> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P123038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Architecture Analysis Method\nA method for analyzing existing software architectures, e.g., to measure or evaluate specific qualities or functions.\n\nArchitecture Design Method\nA method for designing software architectures, e.g., to obtain specific qualities or functions.\n\nArchitecture Optimization Method\nA method to optimize existing architectures (implemented or designed) to regarding specific qualities or properties.\n\nArchitecture Evolution\nThe  process  of  maintaining  and adapting  existing  software architecture to meet requirement and environmental changes [Imran et al., 2016]. This includes papers that investigate the evolution of specific architectures.\n\nArchitecture Description Language\nA formal or software language to create a description of a software architecture, i.e., \"any form of expression for use in architecture descriptions\" [ISO/IEC 42010].\n\nArchitecture Decision Making\nIn software development and evolution, decision-making is an integral part. Thus, various decisions are being made throughout the software development life cycle concerning processes, products, tools, methods, and techniques. From a decision-making perspective, all these questions are confronted by different objectives and constraints, a huge number of variables under dynamically  changing  requirements,  processes,  actors,  stakeholders,  tools  and  techniques. This is combined with incomplete, fuzzy or inconsistent information about all the involved artefacts. [Ruhe2003]\n\nReference Architecture\nA description of an architecture (e.g. domain-specific or to solve recurring problems) that can be tailored to specific use cases.\n\nArchitecture Pattern\nAn architectural pattern is a general, reusable solution to a commonly occurring problem in software architecture within a given context. Patterns with negative effects on the product, i.e., anti-patterns, are also included here. [Taylor et al, 2009]\n\nArchitecture Description\nAn Architecture Description (AD) is a work product used to express the Architecture of some System Of Interest. An AD describes one possible Architecture for a System Of Interest. An AD may take the form of a document, a set of models, a model repository, or some other form [ISO/IEC 42010].\n\nArchitectural Aspects\nA method for identifying or specifying specific architectural aspects in existing implemented architectures, e.g., automatically identifying transactional contexts in an architecture. Note that if you analyse an architecture description containing these aspects, the analysis is a separate research object.\n\nTechnical Debt\n\"In software-intensive systems, technical debt consists of design or implementation constructs that are expedient in the short term, but set up a technical context that can make a future change more costly or impossible. Technical debt is a contingent liability whose impact is limited to internal system qualities, primarily maintainability and evolvability.\" [Avgeriou2016]\n\nArchitecture Extraction\nDesigning and realizing methods and algorithms to automatically extract architecture information from existing implementations.\n\nArchitectural Assumptions\nAssumptions are the reasons for architectural decisions that are more or less arbitrarily taken on the fly because of personal experience, background, domain knowledge, the artifacts reused, and the like [Lago et al., 2005]" .
