<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P142016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P142016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Human-in-Loop approaches are commonly used in situations where automated systems may encounter uncertainty, ambiguity, or complexity beyond their current capabilities. By involving humans in the loop, these systems can leverage human intelligence to address challenging tasks, improve decision-making, and enhance the overall performance and reliability of the system." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P142016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Human-in-Loop" .
