<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157000> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157000> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The participants condition predicate describes the specific health or medical condition of the participants involved in a research study. It highlights the characteristics or status of the individuals taking part in the study regarding their health, illness, injury, or any other relevant condition." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157000> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "participants condition" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The company, organization or team that the SLM is affiliated" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model affiliation" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The main types of attention mechanisms used in SLMs include: 1) Multi-Head Attention (MHA), widely used in transformer models 2) Multi-Query Attention (MQA) using a single shared query across all heads but allowing different key and value projections 3) Group-Query Attention (GQA) sharing query representations across multiple heads while allowing separate key and value representations, and 4) Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) using low-rank key-value joint compression, requiring much less Key-Value (KV) Cache" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "attention" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This field refers to the number of layers in the transformer decoder-only model. Each layer typically consists of a self-attention mechanism followed by a feed-forward neural network (FFN)" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "layer-number" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Boolean value indicating if the SLM has been trained with open source datasets" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "open training datasets" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The maximum context window refers to the maximum number of tokens that a language model can consider at once when processing input data. It defines the length of the input sequence that the model can handle in a single forward pass. In the context of SLMs, the maximum context window varies across different models, ranging from 1k to 128k." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "max context window" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 'wiki' predicate indicates the reference or link to a Wikipedia page that is relevant to the research paper's topic or the entities mentioned in the paper." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P157006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "wiki" .
