<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This predicate describes the integration of the research tools or systems with editors, indicating a feature or capability of the research contribution in the field of science. It signifies the interoperability, compatibility, or collaboration between the tools used in the research and the editors that facilitate writing, editing, or presenting the research findings." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "integration with editors" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Entity generation refers to the process of creating or producing entities, such as data, objects, or elements, within a given domain or context. This predicate describes the generation of new entities as a significant contribution of the research, potentially involving the creation of novel datasets, software, models, or other entities for scientific purposes." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "entity generation" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
