<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Custom Naming Conventions is a research predicate that refers to the unique and tailored naming conventions or naming schemes introduced and utilized in the study to represent entities, variables, concepts, or other elements within the research context. These conventions are often designed to improve clarity, consistency, and organization of data or information in the research project." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P160009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Custom Naming Conventions" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P16000> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
