<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188053> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inference paradigm" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188054> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188054> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188054> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mathematical formulation" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188055> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188055> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188055> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intended use / scope" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188056> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Output artifact" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188057> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188057> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 'literature search method' predicate describes the systematic approach or techniques employed by researchers to identify, select, and review relevant academic and scientific literature related to their study. This includes databases searched, keywords used, inclusion and exclusion criteria, and any tools or protocols followed to ensure a comprehensive and unbiased collection of prior work." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188057> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "literature search method" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188058> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188058> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188058> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Literature search representativeness refers to the extent to which the literature search conducted in a research paper comprehensively and accurately reflects the relevant body of existing knowledge on the topic. It indicates how well the selected literature covers the key studies, theories, and findings pertinent to the research question, ensuring that the review is unbiased, thorough, and representative of the field." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188058> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "literature search representativeness" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188059> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188059> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188059> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Type of evidence refers to the classification or category of data, observations, or information presented in a research paper that supports the study's findings or conclusions. It helps to understand the nature and strength of the proof provided, such as experimental results, statistical analysis, case studies, simulations, or theoretical arguments." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188059> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "type of evidence" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188060> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188060> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188060> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The 'synthesis method' predicate describes the specific technique or process used to create or produce a material, compound, or system in the research. It highlights the methodological approach employed by the researchers to achieve the synthesis, which is central to understanding the novelty, efficiency, or applicability of the research contribution." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188060> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "synthesis method" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188061> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188061> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A reporting guideline is a structured framework or set of criteria designed to improve the transparency, completeness, and quality of research reporting. It helps authors ensure that all essential aspects of their study are clearly and comprehensively documented, facilitating reproducibility and critical appraisal by readers and reviewers." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188061> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reporting guideline" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188062> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188062> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188062> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Quality assessment refers to the systematic evaluation of the quality, reliability, and validity of research methods, data, or results presented in a scientific study. It involves analyzing the strengths and weaknesses of the research to ensure that the findings are credible and can be trusted. This property is crucial for understanding the rigor and robustness of the research contribution." .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188062> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "quality assessment" .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188063> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://orkg.org/orkg/class/Predicate> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188063> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://orkg.org/orkg/predicate/P188063> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The predicate 'update' refers to the process of making changes or improvements to existing methods, models, data, or theories within a research work. It highlights the contribution of the paper in refining, enhancing, or revising prior knowledge or techniques." .
